# chrome tiers (TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.1; TUI-DESIGN-3 §3.2): boxed at 24x80 (the console's top edge carries the badge; the resting mark under
# the rule), flat at 12x60 (no box rows, no wordmark, the status row at column 0), boxed again at 24x80 with the mark back; the shrink segment may cost one clear, the grow none.
# The flat tier is NOT anchored on the badge prefix any more: TUI-DESIGN-2 §1.5 drops that prefix FIRST when the row
# runs short (round 3's `llm-jev` default carried an 18-cell badge that could not fit a 60-column status row; the agent
# default's `agent` fits). The anchor is the flat shape itself — the prompt and status rows with no `|` box edge.
# Every expect precedes the sleep that follows its resize: the driver's `sleep` drains (and consumes) the pty, so a row
# that arrived during a sleep can never be matched afterwards.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*agent
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
resize 12 60
expect \n(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*(?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*Say hi
sleep 0.5
mark shrunk
resize 24 80
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*agent
sleep 0.5
mark grown
send Z
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*Z
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
